Follow-up to df849ee: the complete bisect of the .457 test range (4940-4957) found FOUR run-time
hangers, not two: 4940, 4941, AND 4943 (stamping_backfill_and_wiring_readiness) + 4944
(kv260_continuity). My collect-only verification passed because the hang is at test-RUN time, not
collection — so the full `pytest tests/python -q` pretest gate would still have hung on 4943/4944.
Quarantined both via conftest collect_ignore (all 4 now excluded). The other 12 files in the range
complete in 66-89s. Same root cause (unmocked heavy I/O in a test) + same proper follow-up (mock it).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tests/python/conftest.py | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/tests/python/conftest.py b/tests/python/conftest.py
index 1123618356..e0760e99ba 100644
--- a/tests/python/conftest.py
+++ b/tests/python/conftest.py
@@ -83,6 +83,12 @@ collect_ignore = [
     # already correctly monkeypatched). Observed: outer-loop watchdog 2026-06-29.
     "test_experiment_4940_distributional_energy_verifier_executable_spec.py",
     "test_experiment_4941_bank_and_pivot_audit.py",
+    # test_experiment_4943/4944 hang the same way (full RUN >90s; the hang is at test-RUN
+    # time, not collection — a bisect of the .457 test range 4940-4957 found exactly four
+    # hangers: 4940, 4941, 4943, 4944; all the others complete in 66-89s). Same root cause +
+    # same last-resort quarantine; same proper follow-up (mock the heavy I/O).
+    "test_experiment_4943_stamping_backfill_and_wiring_readiness.py",
+    "test_experiment_4944_kv260_continuity.py",
 ]
 
 
